The operational probes passed on empty, mixed-sign, multi-element, and non-integer cases; the candidate’s non-target slice branch was also checked to delegate to the generated operational function. A deliberately dishonest constant/identity interpretation can make the parameterized target close vacuously, and the probe confirms that—exactly the adversarial case the requested bridge audit must catch. The actual four definitions are structural recurrences/delegations matching the frozen K rules, so they do not exhibit that failure. I’m now running the audit-input-bound final mechanical gate as a last consistency check.
